From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:41:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] feat(desktop): v4 research grid gains the replayed
 ISO-2-alone arm

The last missing cell of the v4 research grid: ISO 15118-2 rules alone
(EV_AI_ISO=1 EV_AI_ISO_VEC=0, SLAC off). It was replayed 2026-09-30 22:25 to
10-01 05:34 on the same frozen tree, weights, split and sessions as the ISO
15118 edition's replay, then rescored per label profile by
ev_charger_ai/benchmark/research_grid_from_cache.py (replay-arm v4-iso2):
- strict.iso2 equals that replay's leaderboard;
- RL (no rule layer) equals baseline in every profile;
- alert for alert, it differs from the ISO-2 + SLAC replay only where the SLAC
  rule fired earlier (plus one AgenticAI memory knock-on).

Strict scores, baseline -> ISO-2 alone -> ISO-2 + SLAC 600 ms:
  TraditionalAI 69.6 -> 70.3 -> 77.3   (the edition's gain is almost all SLAC)
  MultiAgent    60.2 -> 65.1 -> 72.5
  AgenticAI     66.9 -> 69.8 -> 70.9
  AIAgent       46.4 -> 61.0 -> 68.9   (ISO-2 is what rescues AIAgent)

RESEARCH_PROFILES_V4 is regenerated from the pipeline JSON: all 60 existing
cells unchanged, 15 iso2 cells added, and armScoredAt dates the new arm. The
"+ ISO 15118-2" tab is now live for the v4 editions and nothing on the v4
grid reads "not measured". 303 tests pass; tsc is 130 total, 0 in
fault-detection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
